#### Article 5

Child victims of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 4, also obtain special rights, as follows:
a. right to respect;  
b. right to basic services;  
c. right to equal protection;  
d. right to be free from various stigma;  
e. right to obtain freedom;  
f. full right to survival, growth and development.

# CHAPTER IV

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

#### Article 6

Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children in the Region are the joint responsibility of:
a. Regional Government;  
b. community;  
c. family and/or parents.

#### Article 7

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:
   a. implementing protection policies against gender-based violence and children established by the government;
   b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for protection against gender-based violence and children;
   c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection for women and children from violence;  
   d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children;  
   e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children in accordance with regional financial capacity; and
   f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children.
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government establishes action programs and activities for the protection of gender and children in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing protection against gender-based violence and children.  
3. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by a Mayor's Regulation.

#### Article 8

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 6 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.  
2. Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
   a. preventing the occurrence of gender-based violence and children;  
   b. providing information and/or reporting gender-based violence and children to law enforcement or authorized parties; and/or
   c. participating in providing assistance, protection or handling of victims of violence.  
3. Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 9

The obligations and responsibilities of family and/or parents as referred to in Article 6 letter c to prevent all forms of violence and protect victims of gender-based violence and children as family members in accordance with their respective roles.

# CHAPTER V

## DUTIES AND AUTHORITIES OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

#### Article 10

1. The Regional Government has the duty to carry out efforts to prevent the occurrence of gender-based violence and children, in the form of:
   a. collecting data and information about gender-based violence and children, and laws and regulations;
   b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children;  
   c. conducting education on anti-violence values against gender and children; and
   d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children.  
2. The Regional Government in anticipating the occurrence of gender-based violence and children, has the authority to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
   a. providing and facilitating the establishment of integrated services for victims of violence by involving institutions and community elements;  
   b. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims; and
   c. conducting community empowerment for the prevention of violence; and
   d. actively carrying out handling efforts for victims of gender-based violence and children.  
3. The Regional Government in carrying out obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives, or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

# CHAPTER VI

## IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION

## Bagian Kesatu

Institutional

#### Article 11

In order to provide services and protection against gender-based violence and children, the Regional Government establishes the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution (LP PAR) as an integrated service center for victims of gender-based violence and children.

## Bagian Kedua

Forms and Mechanisms of Prevention

#### Article 12

Forms of prevention of gender-based violence and children carried out by the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution, can be implemented through:
a. socialization activities of laws and regulations to the community; and
b. training of members of the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution related to the implementation of their duties in preventing gender-based violence and children.

#### Article 13

1. The Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution in carrying out its duties and functions may coordinate with the Sub-district Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution and competent parties in making efforts to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts of gender-based violence and children.  
2. Further provisions regarding the mechanism for implementing prevention duties as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Mayor's Regulation.

## Bagian Ketiga

Prevention of Violence

#### Article 14

1. The Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts of gender-based violence and children.  
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government makes efforts as follows:
   a. increasing the number and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;  
   b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;  
   c. opening employment opportunities;  
   d. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection against gender-based violence and children;  
   e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;  
   f. building cooperative networks with law enforcement officers, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about gender and children; and
   g. opening complaint posts for protection against gender-based violence and children.

#### Article 15

1. Efforts to prevent the occurrence of gender-based violence and children as referred to in Article 14, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
   a. social affairs;  
   b. health;  
   c. education;  
   d. manpower;  
   e. women's empowerment and child protection;
   f. public order and security; and
   g. planning.  
2. Prevention of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

## Bagian Keempat

Services and Assistance

#### Article 16

Forms of services and assistance for victims of gender-based violence and children organized by the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution, include:
a. medical;  
b. medicolegal;  
c. psychosocial;  
d. legal;  
e. economic independence

## Bagian Kelima

Principles of Services and Assistance

