#### Article 17

The provision of services and assistance to victims of gender-based violence and children shall be carried out with the following principles: a. fast, safe, and empathetic;  
b. guarantee of confidentiality;  
c. easily accessible; and  
d. free of charge.

## Part Six

Services for Victims of Violence

#### Article 18

1. Forms of services shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;  
b. health;  
c. gender-based empowerment and child protection; d. welfare;  
e. education;  
f. population;  
g. labor.  
2. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall cooperate with Government agencies, Provincial Government, other Regency/City Governments, and the community.

#### Article 19

The Regional Government and/or the community may establish recovery houses or safe houses.

## Part Seven

Reunification

#### Article 20

1. Forms of Reunification provided to victims of gender-based violence and children are as follows: a. repatriation/returning home;  
b. social reintegration.  
2. Return services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a include: a. coordinating with relevant agencies;  
b. implementing the victim return process; and c. providing protection to the victim's destination.  
3. Social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b include: a. assistance in the process of reunification with the victim's family;  
b. providing information to the local community for the victim's reunification with their environment;  
c. providing assurance that the family and community are ready to accept the victim back; and d. implementing economic empowerment.

## Part Eight

Empowerment of Victims of Violence

#### Article 21

1. The Regional Government is obligated to empower victims of violence.  
2. Empowerment of victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution.  
3. In empowering victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall prepare empowerment programs in the economic field, which include: a. providing the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for victims of violence, in order to increase knowledge, attitudes, and business skills;  
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;  
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;  
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop businesses of victims of violence;  
e. facilitating the provision of capital for victims of violence; and f. expanding access to information and promoting the products of victims of violence.  
4. In empowering victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

#### Article 22

1. Empowerment of victims of violence as referred to in Article 21 shall be carried out by providing training to improve capabilities, skills, and independence.  
2. Training as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted through: a. on-the-job training;  
b. pre-placement training; and c. job-ready training.

#### Article 23

Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties and functions of the Women, Children and Youth Protection Institution and the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

# CHAPTER VII

## COOPERATION AND PARTNERSHIP

## Part One

Cooperation

#### Article 24

1. In order to achieve the objectives of implementing protection against gender-based violence and children as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government shall cooperate with: a. the Government;  
b. the Provincial Government;  
c. other regency/city governments; and d. the community.  
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;  
b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;  
c. return and social reintegration; and d. provision of evidence and witnesses, and followed up in accordance with applicable law.  
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with laws and regulations.

## Part Two

Partnership

#### Article 25

1. The Regional Government shall establish partnerships with stakeholders in the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children.  
2. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted through: a. notification of job opportunity information for victims of gender-based violence and children;  
b. education and training for victims of violence; c. educational assistance for victims of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; and d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of victims of violence.  
3. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of an agreement.

# CHAPTER VIII

## GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

#### Article 26

1. The Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children.  
2. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. minimum service standards (SPM);  
b. technical guidance and training;  
c. provision of facilities;  
d. monitoring; and e. evaluation.  
3. Supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted with the following principles: a. professional;  
b. transparent; and c. accountable.  
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for guidance and supervision by the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (2) and paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

#### Article 27

The community may supervise the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children organized by the Regional Government through the mechanism of conveying aspirations to the Mayor or DPRD.

# CHAPTER IX

## COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

#### Article 28

1. The community may participate in efforts to implement protection against gender-based violence and children. (2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals or organizations.  
3. Community participation in the implementation of protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children may be carried out through: a. providing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children;  
b. providing emergency assistance;  
c. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of cases of gender-based violence and children;  
d. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders;  
e. conveying information to the competent authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and children; f. fostering local wisdom with the principles of non-discrimination and the best interests of victims in handling gender-based violence and children;  
g. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and children; h. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and children.

# CHAPTER X

## REPORTING

#### Article 29

1. SKPD is obligated to report the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and children to the Mayor.  
2. Reporting as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be submitted in writing, including: a. administration;  
b. finance;  
c. services; and d. performance.  
3. Submission of written reports on recapitulation of reported cases shall be carried out at least once every 3 (three) months.
